      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "FIVE LAYERS \u00b7 THREE GROUPINGS \u00b7 ONE SET OF DETECTIONS",
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "FIVE LAYERS \u00b7 THREE GROUPINGS \u00b7 ONE SET OF DETECTIONS",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t0180",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 78,
      "y": 1158.75,
      "width": 835.1999999999999,
      "height": 345.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#212529",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g0177"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 868285354,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 825635098,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "                              ONE L2B GRANULE CARRIES TWO MINERAL IDs\n     Tetracorder assigns at most ONE constituent per group per pixel - so a granule is two id bands, not 294.\n\n        group 1   ~1 um, electronic absorptions                group 2   2.0-2.5 um, vibrational overtones\n                  iron oxides, Fe-bearing silicates                      clays, micas, carbonates, sulfates\n                            |                                                        |\n              +-------------+-------------+                     +-------------+------+------+--------------+\n              |                           |                     |                           |              |\n        mineral_1_native            iron_oxide            mineral_2_native            alteration    mineral_family\n        classes: source             @ref:iron-oxide-v1    classes: source             @ref:          @ref:mineral-\n        the product's own           goethite / hematite   the product's own           alteration-v1  family-v1\n        294 rows, no lumping        / jarosite first      294 rows, no lumping        the deposit-   the same rows,\n                                                                                      system cut     cut differently\n\n  THREE GROUPINGS OVER THE SAME DETECTIONS, each an independent enumeration and an independent vote. None is\n  privileged; a fourth is a YAML file. \"The only way to do this is to basically flood it and give multiple\n  different groupings available.\"   The ungrouped 294-class layers ship BESIDE the groupings, not instead of\n  them, because a picture of the raw detections is what tells you whether a grouping threw something away.\n\n  NO GROUP-1 / GROUP-2 TRADE.  joint_mineral_vote would answer a cell from group 2 where group 2 voted and\n  from group 1 where it did not.  The 17 Sep tag-up ruled that out: \"the detections between group one and\n  group 2 are independent from one another... you cannot swap in a group 2 if a group one is absent.\"\n  Two mosaics, never one.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "                              ONE L2B GRANULE CARRIES TWO MINERAL IDs\n     Tetracorder assigns at most ONE constituent per group per pixel - so a granule is two id bands, not 294.\n\n        group 1   ~1 um, electronic absorptions                group 2   2.0-2.5 um, vibrational overtones\n                  iron oxides, Fe-bearing silicates                      clays, micas, carbonates, sulfates\n                            |                                                        |\n              +-------------+-------------+                     +-------------+------+------+--------------+\n              |                           |                     |                           |              |\n        mineral_1_native            iron_oxide            mineral_2_native            alteration    mineral_family\n        classes: source             @ref:iron-oxide-v1    classes: source             @ref:          @ref:mineral-\n        the product's own           goethite / hematite   the product's own           alteration-v1  family-v1\n        294 rows, no lumping        / jarosite first      294 rows, no lumping        the deposit-   the same rows,\n                                                                                      system cut     cut differently\n\n  THREE GROUPINGS OVER THE SAME DETECTIONS, each an independent enumeration and an independent vote. None is\n  privileged; a fourth is a YAML file. \"The only way to do this is to basically flood it and give multiple\n  different groupings available.\"   The ungrouped 294-class layers ship BESIDE the groupings, not instead of\n  them, because a picture of the raw detections is what tells you whether a grouping threw something away.\n\n  NO GROUP-1 / GROUP-2 TRADE.  joint_mineral_vote would answer a cell from group 2 where group 2 voted and\n  from group 1 where it did not.  The 17 Sep tag-up ruled that out: \"the detections between group one and\n  group 2 are independent from one another... you cannot swap in a group 2 if a group one is absent.\"\n  Two mosaics, never one.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
