      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "SCORING \u00b7 which look wins the cell, within one week",
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "SCORING \u00b7 which look wins the cell, within one week",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t0184",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1338,
      "y": 1158.75,
      "width": 521.4,
      "height": 330.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#212529",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g0181"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2018026271,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2088043438,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "score  =  soil  +  0.25 * cos(theta_sun)  +  0.10 * (1 - |theta_view| / 15 deg)\n           ^^^^     ^^^^                      ^^^^\n           COVER    illumination breaks       look geometry breaks\n           DECIDES  ties among comparable     what illumination\n                    ground                    leaves\n\nsun_weight + nadir_weight <= 1 is ENFORCED in the constructor, so the two\ntie-breakers can never outrank the term that matters. nadir_weight: 0\nreproduces prefer_bare_earth exactly.\n\nNaN - \"this observation may not occupy this cell\" - not a low score:\n    soil < 0.65  (hard_floor)   the grain-size retrieval falls apart\n    theta_sun  > 80 deg         the sun cannot light the surface\n    theta_view > 90 deg\n\nmin_soil 0.80 is kept SEPARATE from hard_floor 0.65, so the 0.65-0.80\nband still RANKS instead of being discarded.\n\nMeasured, one tile over all of 2025: the nadir term recovers 0.36 deg of\nthe 1.57 deg mean view zenith that prefer_bare_earth gives away, and drops\nthe share of cells taking a >2 deg worse look from 34 % to 26 %, at no cost\nto illumination. It changes the mineral label on 0.08 % of cells - so this\nis a TILE-CONTINUITY knob, not a correctness fix. Worth saying plainly,\nbecause the obvious assumption is the opposite.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "score  =  soil  +  0.25 * cos(theta_sun)  +  0.10 * (1 - |theta_view| / 15 deg)\n           ^^^^     ^^^^                      ^^^^\n           COVER    illumination breaks       look geometry breaks\n           DECIDES  ties among comparable     what illumination\n                    ground                    leaves\n\nsun_weight + nadir_weight <= 1 is ENFORCED in the constructor, so the two\ntie-breakers can never outrank the term that matters. nadir_weight: 0\nreproduces prefer_bare_earth exactly.\n\nNaN - \"this observation may not occupy this cell\" - not a low score:\n    soil < 0.65  (hard_floor)   the grain-size retrieval falls apart\n    theta_sun  > 80 deg         the sun cannot light the surface\n    theta_view > 90 deg\n\nmin_soil 0.80 is kept SEPARATE from hard_floor 0.65, so the 0.65-0.80\nband still RANKS instead of being discarded.\n\nMeasured, one tile over all of 2025: the nadir term recovers 0.36 deg of\nthe 1.57 deg mean view zenith that prefer_bare_earth gives away, and drops\nthe share of cells taking a >2 deg worse look from 34 % to 26 %, at no cost\nto illumination. It changes the mineral label on 0.08 % of cells - so this\nis a TILE-CONTINUITY knob, not a correctness fix. Worth saying plainly,\nbecause the obvious assumption is the opposite.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
