      "text": "REDUCING \u00b7 how 52 weeks become one answer",
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "REDUCING \u00b7 how 52 weeks become one answer",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t0188",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1968,
      "y": 1158.75,
      "width": 528.0,
      "height": 330.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#212529",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "g0185"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1513921164,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2105486678,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CATEGORICAL - vote, \"mode through time\".  The voting unit is the EPOCH, not the\nobservation: a week with four looks casts ONE vote, cast by the look the scorer\nliked best. That is what stops a cloudy fortnight outvoting a clear year.\n    1  discard invalid epochs                       -> n_epochs\n    2  drop `ignore: [none]` from the TALLY, but NOT from n_epochs\n    3  take the modal class\n    4  suppress to nodata where the modal count < min_count (3)\n    5  break ties on the single highest score any tied class holds\n  ->  <layer>                 the winner\n      <layer>_agreement       modal count / n_epochs - reported even where\n                              min_count suppressed the winner, because it\n                              describes the TALLY, not the decision\n      <layer>_runner_up       the second class, under the same tie rule\n\nCONTINUOUS - median, and this is the part worth reading twice.  `conditional_on`\nnarrows the epoch set to those whose categorical value EQUALS the winner, so\ndepth_1 is the median band depth OF THE MINERAL THAT WON - not the median of\nwhatever was in that cell each week. spread: iqr ships the disagreement.\n  ->  depth_1 \u00b7 depth_1_n \u00b7 depth_1_iqr\n\nWeekly, not monthly, and the reason is EMIT's clustered revisit: under a monthly\nepoch two looks in one month collapse to one vote and the loser is DISCARDED.\nMeasured on the pilot tile, halving the epoch recovered +19.8 % of classified\narea in group 1 and +25.8 % in group 2 at the same min_count.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CATEGORICAL - vote, \"mode through time\".  The voting unit is the EPOCH, not the\nobservation: a week with four looks casts ONE vote, cast by the look the scorer\nliked best. That is what stops a cloudy fortnight outvoting a clear year.\n    1  discard invalid epochs                       -> n_epochs\n    2  drop `ignore: [none]` from the TALLY, but NOT from n_epochs\n    3  take the modal class\n    4  suppress to nodata where the modal count < min_count (3)\n    5  break ties on the single highest score any tied class holds\n  ->  <layer>                 the winner\n      <layer>_agreement       modal count / n_epochs - reported even where\n                              min_count suppressed the winner, because it\n                              describes the TALLY, not the decision\n      <layer>_runner_up       the second class, under the same tie rule\n\nCONTINUOUS - median, and this is the part worth reading twice.  `conditional_on`\nnarrows the epoch set to those whose categorical value EQUALS the winner, so\ndepth_1 is the median band depth OF THE MINERAL THAT WON - not the median of\nwhatever was in that cell each week. spread: iqr ships the disagreement.\n  ->  depth_1 \u00b7 depth_1_n \u00b7 depth_1_iqr\n\nWeekly, not monthly, and the reason is EMIT's clustered revisit: under a monthly\nepoch two looks in one month collapse to one vote and the loser is DISCARDED.\nMeasured on the pilot tile, halving the epoch recovered +19.8 % of classified\narea in group 1 and +25.8 % in group 2 at the same min_count.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
