      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CACHING - every derived thing is content-addressed and lives in S3: the GLT, the masked observation, the ortho and aux warps, the epoch snapshot,\nthe product block. Verbatim DAAC granules are the one exception and stay node-local, because an unmodified copy in S3 buys nothing. So a re-run resumes\nonto whatever survived, and widening the window to 2026 re-reads the 2025 snapshots instead of recomputing them - as long as the scorer, the masks and\nthe schema still hash the same. That last clause is the whole contract.\n\nMEASURED, not estimated, against CMR on 17 Sep 2026:   1,932 granules \u00b7 402 tiles \u00b7 9,233 regrid \u00b7 87,479 resolve \u00b7 10,050 reduce \u00b7 402 publish\n                                                       ~442 GB in \u00b7 ~845 GB of S3 at peak \u00b7 ~$33-92 of Lambda \u00b7 ~85-193 CPU-hours\n\nBoxes are clickable: each links to the code or the manifest line that implements it, pinned at 1ececcf so the line numbers stay true.\nGenerated from examples/emit-us-west-2025/manifest.yaml - and then hand-edited, so this file is the source of truth, not the generator.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CACHING - every derived thing is content-addressed and lives in S3: the GLT, the masked observation, the ortho and aux warps, the epoch snapshot,\nthe product block. Verbatim DAAC granules are the one exception and stay node-local, because an unmodified copy in S3 buys nothing. So a re-run resumes\nonto whatever survived, and widening the window to 2026 re-reads the 2025 snapshots instead of recomputing them - as long as the scorer, the masks and\nthe schema still hash the same. That last clause is the whole contract.\n\nMEASURED, not estimated, against CMR on 17 Sep 2026:   1,932 granules \u00b7 402 tiles \u00b7 9,233 regrid \u00b7 87,479 resolve \u00b7 10,050 reduce \u00b7 402 publish\n                                                       ~442 GB in \u00b7 ~845 GB of S3 at peak \u00b7 ~$33-92 of Lambda \u00b7 ~85-193 CPU-hours\n\nBoxes are clickable: each links to the code or the manifest line that implements it, pinned at 1ececcf so the line numbers stay true.\nGenerated from examples/emit-us-west-2025/manifest.yaml - and then hand-edited, so this file is the source of truth, not the generator.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
